+
+/** Same as get_physfs_SDLRWops(), except that the file is read into memory first
+    and the returned stream seeks inside that buffer.
+
+    Needed because PhysFS cannot seek within a deflate-compressed zip entry: a
+    backwards seek rewinds the entry and re-inflates it up to the target offset
+    (physfs_archiver_zip.c, ZIP_seek()). FreeType opens a font by seeking to the
+    sfnt table directory and then back to each table, so loading a font straight
+    out of the compressed data.zip costs one full re-inflation per backwards seek
+    -- measured at 3.3 s for the 16.5 MB NotoSansCJKjp-Medium.otf. LanguageMenu
+    builds a TTFFont for every language that needs a custom font, and cmn, ja,
+    zh_CN and zh_TW all map to that one file, so the menu spent ~14 s on the main
+    thread and HarmonyOS's watchdog killed the app (THREAD_BLOCK_6S + SIGKILL).
+
+    Buffers are cached per filename, so those four languages share a single copy
+    instead of decompressing the file four times. The stream does not own the
+    buffer; the cache keeps it alive for the lifetime of the process. */
+SDL_IOStream* get_physfs_SDLRWops_memory(const std::string& filename);
+
 SDL_IOStream* get_writable_physfs_SDLRWops(const std::string& filename);
